<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5350" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭmăris</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		bis - mare, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>lying between two seas.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, an epithet of Corinth (<b>poet.</b>; a favorite word of Ovid): bimarisve
			Corinthi Moenia, * <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1, 7, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5,
				407</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ephyre,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. H.
					12, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Isthmos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					7, 405</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">6, 419</span></i> sq.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">morbus,</span>”
				<i>of one who practises unnatural unchastity</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Epigr. 131</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
